# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# TikuC: the same place to work, wearing its other name.  What differs
# is what it puts FORWARD -- no Run row, because nothing here runs a C
# program yet, and Build offered without being asked, because asking
# the compiler is what this program is for.  A project that names no
# target is asked about on this machine.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Programming
wait 4
expect-menu TikuC
menu-pick TikuC
wait 25
note it announces itself under its own name
expect-title TikuC
wait 200
expect-no-title TikuC
expect-title Project
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
expect-title TikuTracker: Open
click 400 248
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
note no Run row -- Add File… sits beside Build, and Build needs no
note target line to be offered.  And no About row here: that went
note where the system keeps its own, wearing this program's name
click-window Project
wait 8
click 20 8
wait 8
expect-menu About TikuC
note a click on open ground puts the strip's menu away
click 500 600
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Add File…|Build for host|Close Project
menu-pick Build for host
wait 200
expect-title Messages
key Down
wait 8
key Down
wait 10
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Go to line 4
menu-pick Go to line 4
wait 120
expect-title bad.c
key x shift
wait 10
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Save bad.c
wait 90
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/bad.c Xreturn nope
